{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And it shall cease.</b> For when Sennacherib came he captured Damascus as well as Samaria and its fortresses." "<b>And the remnant of Aram.</b> Since Damascus is the city of Aram, their glory shall be like the glory of the children of Israel, for afterward it is written, \"the glory of Jacob shall be impoverished.\" And some say: \"and the remnant of Aram\" shall be so utterly in disgrace that it shall be as glory for Israel, corresponding to their lot."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:04.566189688Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}